ASoC: sophgo: cv1800b: local fixes for the machine-card integration

Two local fixes on top of the original driver submission (which shipped
without any machine driver or DTS wiring):

1. cv1800b-tdm: accept a zero set_sysclk frequency. When the audio is
   wired up with a simple-audio-card that sets mclk-fs, the ASoC core
   calls snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(cpu_dai, 0, 0, ...) on stream shutdown
   to release the clock. cv1800b_i2s_dai_set_sysclk() forwarded the zero
   frequency into the mclk divider math, where cv1800b_calc_mclk_div()
   returns -EINVAL, so the machine hw_params/shutdown path failed with
   -22 and capture never ran. Treat a zero frequency as "nothing to do".

2. cv1800b-sound-adc: fix the capture rate running exactly 2x too fast.
   The ADC BCLK divider formula carried a spurious *2 in the divisor:
   with the 12.288 MHz MCLK at 48 kHz it computed a divider of 4
   (BCLK 3.072 MHz, LRCK = BCLK/32 = 96 kHz), so a 10 s recording
   completed in 5.0 s of wall time and played back an octave high.
   Removing the *2 doubles the divider (BCLK 1.536 MHz) and yields a
   true 48 kHz frame clock.

Local fixes (candidates for upstream); not part of the original driver
submission.

Signed-off-by: d622 <300083818+d622-au@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/sound/soc/sophgo/cv1800b-tdm.c b/sound/soc/sophgo/cv1800b-tdm.c
